Done. Summary of changes:

**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact-match via `==` (not substring), preserves relative order (single `iter().filter()` pass).

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — `list` command now parses an optional `--tag <TAG>` flag and, when present, routes output through `filter_by_tag`; otherwise lists all notes. Added `Note` to the `use notekeep::{...}` import.

Verified:
- `cargo build` — clean.
- `cargo test` — 2/2 pass.
- CLI end-to-end: `list --tag work` returns only notes tagged exactly `work` in insertion order; `--tag groceries` matches that tag; a nonexistent tag returns empty; and `--tag wo` (a substring of "work") returns nothing, confirming exact matching.

One behavior worth noting: `--tag` with no following value (e.g. `list --tag` at end of args) is treated as no filter (lists all) rather than an error — consistent with the rest of the CLI.


